1
00:00:07,870 --> 00:00:10,560
Welcome to the Watermill Inn.

2
00:00:10,560 --> 00:00:11,360
Oh, Richard,

3
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:13,910
it's exactly as it was when we were married!

4
00:00:13,910 --> 00:00:16,520
And when I got married.

5
00:00:16,520 --> 00:00:19,230
Even the old patchwork quilt is the same!

6
00:00:19,230 --> 00:00:22,170
My great-grandmother made that quilt

7
00:00:22,170 --> 00:00:24,540
when Teddy Roosevelt was President.

8
00:00:24,540 --> 00:00:26,960
In those days, when they made quilts.

9
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:31,150
they cut patches

10
00:00:31,150 --> 00:00:33,510
so that each one would be a part of it.

11
00:00:33,510 --> 00:00:34,980
What a lovely tradition!

12
00:00:34,980 --> 00:00:36,930
Thank you for calling us.

13
00:00:36,930 --> 00:00:40,860
I remember you and your wife

14
00:00:40,860 --> 00:00:42,660
We were very young.

15
00:00:42,660 --> 00:00:45,220
And very much in love.

16
00:00:45,220 --> 00:00:46,890
We have a baby now.

17
00:00:46,890 --> 00:00:50,450
How wonderful! A boy or a girl?

18
00:00:50,450 --> 00:00:52,800
A boy--Max.

19
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:54,500
Do you have a picture?

20
00:00:54,500 --> 00:01:00,280
Would a professional photographer be without a picture?

21
00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:03,150
Oh, he's adorable!

22
00:01:03,150 --> 00:01:04,430
And very bright.

23
00:01:04,430 --> 00:01:06,550
Like his father. A real Stewart.

24
00:01:06,550 --> 00:01:09,020
And very good-looking, like his mother.

25
00:01:09,020 --> 00:01:11,230
Well, it's nice to have you with us again.

26
00:01:11,230 --> 00:01:13,620
Next time, bring the baby.

27
00:01:13,620 --> 00:01:15,790
You see, Richard? Max is welcome here.

28
00:01:15,790 --> 00:01:17,620
Not on our anniversary.

29
00:01:17,620 --> 00:01:20,270
This vacation is for you and me.

30
00:01:20,270 --> 00:01:22,730
If there's anything you need, please call me.

31
00:01:22,730 --> 00:01:27,230
I'll be in the front office all day.

32
00:01:27,230 --> 00:01:35,850
Oh, I took the liberty of ordering some breakfast for you.

33
00:01:35,850 --> 00:01:54,300
Just put it over there, Charles.

34
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:57,450
Thank you, Charles.

35
00:01:57,450 --> 00:01:59,970
Compliments of the Watermill Inn.

36
00:01:59,970 --> 00:02:00,610
Thank you.

37
00:02:00,610 --> 00:02:05,870
Thank you so much.

38
00:02:05,870 --> 00:02:09,680
Now, this is my idea of a good time.

39
00:02:09,680 --> 00:02:17,040
Let's see ... hotcakes and maple syrup, with scrambled eggs.

40
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:20,880
Umm ... smell that coffee ... cinnamon and cloves.

41
00:02:20,880 --> 00:02:23,230
Homemade buttermilk biscuits.

42
00:02:23,230 --> 00:02:26,820
Slices of orange with burnt honey.

43
00:02:26,820 --> 00:02:28,470
Let's eat!

44
00:02:28,470 --> 00:02:29,570
First I want to call home

45
00:02:29,570 --> 00:02:31,380
and check on your mother and the baby.

46
00:02:31,380 --> 00:02:32,750
Honey, if there were any problems,

47
00:02:32,750 --> 00:02:34,140
she would call us.

48
00:02:34,140 --> 00:02:36,330
She doesn't know we've changed hotels.

49
00:02:36,330 --> 00:02:46,150
You're right. Of course.

50
00:02:46,150 --> 00:02:48,340
Hello, operator.

51
00:02:48,340 --> 00:02:56,990
I'd like to call Riverdale, New York.

52
00:02:56,990 --> 00:03:00,480
This food is heavenly, isn't it?

53
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:11,540
This whole place is heavenly.

54
00:03:11,540 --> 00:03:14,980
Do you remember that old desk?

55
00:03:14,980 --> 00:03:17,490
Mrs. Montefiore told me that

56
00:03:17,490 --> 00:03:18,940
George Washington sat at that desk

57
00:03:18,940 --> 00:03:21,730
and wrote to his wife Martha.

58
00:03:21,730 --> 00:03:24,430
What do you want to do after breakfast?

59
00:03:24,430 --> 00:03:27,080
Why don't we take a walk down to the river?

60
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:28,330
In the rain?

61
00:03:28,330 --> 00:03:36,680
No. Look out the window. The sun is shining!

62
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:39,680
Now this is my idea of a good time!
